          "path": "_m/9/x/0/y/heber-valley-railroad-wp/great-western-ry-gp9-2.jpg",
          "filename": "Great Western RY GP9 296.jpg",
          "caption": "Great Western RY GP9 296. Built in  1954 for the Union Pacific and served as its #296 until 1985 when it was sold to the GW.  It last served   the GW  from 1998 to 2003 as a switch engine at Longmont, Colorado.\nI spotted the engine as we drove along Valmont in Boulder. Colorado.  Going back the next day, we found it was the site of Boulder Railroad Historical Society.  We met a friendly man who supplied printed info and interesting comments.\n\nI was impressed with the restoration on several pieces of railroad historical equipment  and will be posting  photos later.",
          "alt": "Great Western RY GP9 296. Built in  1954 for the Union Pacific and served as its #296 until 1985 when it was sold to the GW.  It last served   the GW  from 1998 to 2003 as a switch engine at Longmont, Colorado.\nI spotted the engine as we drove along Valmont in Boulder. Colorado.  Going back the next day, we found it was the site of Boulder Railroad Historical Society.  We met a friendly man who supplied printed info and interesting comments.\n\nI was impressed with the restoration on several pieces of railroad historical equipment  and will be posting  photos later.",
